From: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: tear flows down when a device MTU changes

Tear down the offloaded flows of a device whose MTU changes.
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c
@@ -824,7 +824,10 @@ static int nf_flow_table_netdev_event(st
 {
 	struct net_device *dev = netdev_notifier_info_to_dev(ptr);
 
-	if (event != NETDEV_DOWN)
+	/* A flow carries the MTU of its path from its creation on: tear it
+	 * down so that it is set up again with the new one.
+	 */
+	if (event != NETDEV_DOWN && event != NETDEV_CHANGEMTU)
 		return NOTIFY_DONE;
 
 	nf_flow_table_cleanup(dev);
